│     ├─1 inlineCode "nested-string-quote-style = \"preferred\""
│     └─2 text ",\nRuff will use the configured quote style for nested strings:"
├─121 code "f\"outer f-string {f\"nested f-string {f\"another nested f-string\"} end\"} end\""
│       lang: "python"
│       meta: null
├─122 heading[1]
│     │ depth: 4
│     └─0 text "Line breaks"
├─123 paragraph[5]
│     ├─0 text "Starting with Python 3.12 ("
│     ├─1 link[1]
│     │   │ title: null
│     │   │ url: "https://peps.python.org/pep-0701/"
│     │   └─0 text "PEP 701"
│     ├─2 text "), the expression parts of an f-string can\nspan multiple lines. Ruff needs to decide when to introduce a line break in an f-string expression.\nThis depends on the semantic content of the expression parts of an f-string - for example,\nintroducing a line break in the middle of a natural-language sentence is undesirable. Since Ruff\ndoesn't have enough information to make that decision, it adopts a heuristic similar to "
│     ├─3 link[1]
│     │   │ title: null
│     │   │ url: "https://prettier.io/docs/en/next/rationale.html#template-literals"
│     │   └─0 text "Prettier"
│     └─4 text ":\nit will only split the expression parts of an f-string across multiple lines if there was already a line break\nwithin any of the expression parts."
├─124 paragraph[1]
│     └─0 text "For example, the following code:"
├─125 code "f\"this f-string has a multiline expression {\n  ['red', 'green', 'blue', 'yellow',]} and does not fit within the line length\""
│       lang: "python"
│       meta: null
├─126 paragraph[1]
│     └─0 text "... is formatted as:"
├─127 code "# The list expression is split across multiple lines because of the trailing comma\nf\"this f-string has a multiline expression {\n    [\n        'red',\n        'green',\n        'blue',\n        'yellow',\n    ]\n} and does not fit within the line length\""
│       lang: "python"
│       meta: null
├─128 paragraph[1]
│     └─0 text "But, the following will not be split across multiple lines even though it exceeds the line length:"
├─129 code "f\"this f-string has a multiline expression {['red', 'green', 'blue', 'yellow']} and does not fit within the line length\""
│       lang: "python"
│       meta: null
├─130 paragraph[3]
│     ├─0 text "If you want Ruff to split an f-string across multiple lines, ensure there's a linebreak somewhere within the\n"
│     ├─1 inlineCode "{...}"
│     └─2 text " parts of an f-string."
